# Base Rules (load-bearing)

Most sessions run unattended. A session manager or scheduler hands you a work item, and nobody watches the chat. A flow runs to its end without prompts, is safe to re-run, and returns `recovery-required` instead of guessing when input is missing. Humans act only at exterior gates ([reference/factory-model.md](factory-model-reference.mdc)).

Fix the work, not the gate. Do not weaken, skip, or lower a failing hook, check, threshold, or test, and do not bypass hooks (`--no-verify`, `HUSKY=0`) or branch protection. Green CI is done.

- Use conventional commits, one logical change each. Do not commit directly to `dev`, `staging`, or `main`.
- Rewrite pushed history only with approval, using `--force-with-lease=<ref>:<sha>` for the exact tip approved. If the remote moved, the approval is void.
- Merge with `gh pr merge --merge`. Squash strips the `[skip ci]` markers that promotion detection reads.
- Drive each PR you open to merge, watch its deploy, and include the PR URL when you mention it.
- Add a lint or type suppression only when the tool is wrong, with the reason on the same line.
- Leave dependency directories, untracked files, and `CHANGELOG` alone.

Full prose: [reference/base-rules.md](base-rules-reference.mdc).
